Package: OMICstudio
Title: Interactive Local Multi-Omics Analysis Studio
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("OMICstudio", "Authors", email = "noreply@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A localhost-first, browser-based interactive application for
    multi-omics analysis. Users launch the app with a single command, pick an
    omics type, and work through that pipeline step by step -- entirely on their
    own machine, with no cloud server. The single-cell RNA-seq pipeline is
    complete: twenty steps from import and quality control through doublet
    removal, normalization, dimensionality reduction, batch integration,
    clustering, embedding, markers, annotation, enrichment, trajectory, RNA
    velocity, cell-cycle and signature scoring, cell-cell communication, CNV /
    malignancy inference, survival analysis, visualization, a narrated report
    and export. Bulk RNA-seq, whole-exome sequencing, spatial transcriptomics
    and multi-omics integration are on the roadmap and show their planned steps
    in the interface. Every step offers method alternatives, adjustable
    thresholds, a beginner-friendly explanation, a result summary, a large
    preview plot, and reproducible parameter logging.
